<template>
  <section>
    <h2 class="pdx-txt-heading section-heading">Contrast is built in, not checked afterwards</h2>
    <p class="pdx-txt-small pdx-ink-muted">
      Every figure below is computed <strong>in this page, right now</strong>, by the same
      <code>wcagContrast</code> the theme gate runs — reading the tokens of the theme you are
      currently viewing. Change the theme in the header and the numbers change with it.
    </p>
    <p class="pdx-txt-small pdx-ink-muted">
      The rule: a coloured fill carries a <strong>white</strong> label, and when white cannot reach
      WCAG AA (4.5:1) the <em>fill</em> is darkened until it can — the label is not swapped for a dark
      one. <code>warning</code> is the single exception: a pale yellow no white will ever survive, so
      it carries a dark label by design.
    </p>

    <div class="contrast-table">
      <div class="ct-head">
        <span>Fill token</span><span>Label token</span><span>Ratio</span><span>AA</span>
      </div>
      @for (contrast as row; track row.token) {
        <div class="ct-row" data-contrast-row :data-token="row.token" :data-text-token="row.textToken" :data-ratio="row.ratio">
          <span class="ct-chip" :style="'background: var(' + row.token + '); color: var(' + row.textToken + ')'">Label</span>
          <code class="pdx-txt-mono ct-code">{{ row.token }}</code>
          <code class="pdx-txt-mono ct-code">{{ row.textToken }}</code>
          <span class="ct-ratio">{{ row.ratio }}:1</span>
          <span :class="row.pass ? 'ct-verdict ok' : 'ct-verdict bad'">{{ row.pass ? 'AA' : 'fail' }}</span>
        </div>
      }
    </div>
    <p class="pdx-txt-caption pdx-ink-muted">
      Computed with <code>wcagContrast(parseColorToken(fill), parseColorToken(label))</code> from
      <code>@pdxui/design/engine</code> — the function <code>createTheme().validate()</code> and
      <code>pdx theme --strict</code> use to fail a build.
    </p>
  </section>
</template>

<script setup>
import { useThemeMeasure } from './state.pdx';

// Measured by the page on mount and on every theme change (state.pdx.ts).
const themeMeasure = useThemeMeasure();
const contrast = $derived(themeMeasure.contrast());
</script>

